穿云 core muse.16: REALITY picks its key share by fingerprint and retries once with the other one.
Fixed modern fingerprints that pair X25519MLKEM768 natively (chrome) keep it;
randomized and other specs send plain X25519 again (randomized specs could
add the post-quantum share without listing the group, so about half the
handshakes failed). The auth key always comes from the X25519 share.
A failed REALITY handshake is redialed once with the other mode (vless
direct, TLS dialer transports, xhttp); the mode that works is cached per
server in memory. Paths without a redial switch the next connection.

